1a_math_i_calculus_p_series_0896d7ca_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Does $\\displaystyle\\sum_{n = 1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{n^2}$ converge?","options":["No, because every $p$-series diverges.","No, because $p = 2$ is too large.","Yes, because $p = 2 \\gt 1$.","Yes, because $p = 1$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"63092bfad1580187f1650e7c"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_p_series_0896d7ca_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Does $\\displaystyle\\sum_{n = 1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{n}$ converge?","options":["No, because $p = 1$.","Yes, because $p = 1$.","Yes, because all terms are positive.","No, because $p \\gt 1$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9634eda0ffb7403fd0dedaac"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_p_series_0896d7ca_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What aspect of a $p$-series determines its convergence behaviour?","options":["The first term only.","The exponent $p$.","The notation used for the index.","Whether the symbol $p$ is written in bold."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5e8c34e79eb790f9f3358207"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_p_series_0896d7ca_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Does $\\sum_{n\\ge1} 1/n^{p}$ converge or diverge when $p\\le1$?","options":["$\\displaystyle\\sum_{n = 1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{n^p}$ converges absolutely.","$\\displaystyle\\sum_{n = 1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{n^p}$ converges only when $p = 1$.","$\\displaystyle\\sum_{n = 1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{n^p}$ is finite because it has finitely many terms.","$\\displaystyle\\sum_{n = 1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{n^p}$ diverges."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"658bb24281a4c1a454551662"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_p_series_0896d7ca_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Determine the convergence of $\\displaystyle\\sum_{n = 1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{n^{3/2}}$.","options":["It converg